From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] oleaut32: type library writing stubs, per-user registration, help string DLLs, variable Invoke

Writing type libraries (ICreateTypeLib2/ICreateTypeInfo2), stubs that
returned E_NOTIMPL:
- CreateTypeLib (it failed) gives the writer's ICreateTypeLib.
- DeleteTypeInfo takes a type info out by name; the ones after it move
  down, and the references to them with them.
- SetHelpStringContext on the library is kept and saved (the header's
  field was written as 0); reading takes the header's help context and
  help string context each from its own field (the help string context
  was read as the help context).
- DefineFuncAsDllEntry makes a module's function a DLL entry (by name or
  ordinal), which GetDllEntry gives back.
- DeleteVarDesc, DeleteVarDescByMemId, DeleteFuncDescByMemId.
- SetFuncCustData, SetParamCustData, SetVarCustData,
  SetImplTypeCustData; parameters' and implemented interfaces' custom
  data are now written to the file too.
- SetFuncHelpStringContext, SetVarHelpStringContext; SetMops and
  Invalidate are accepted (nothing to keep, as documented).
- LayOut gives a record's or union's variables their instance offsets
  and the type its instance size (documented; they were left at 0).

Reading and using them:
- GetLibStatistics (a stub that said 1 and 1) counts the library's
  distinct names and their characters.
- GetDocumentation2 (a "partially implemented stub") takes help strings
  from the library's help string DLL (DLLGetDocumentation) when it has
  one, and gives the library's help string context; a type info's help
  string is its documentation string, not its name.
- ITypeInfo::Invoke of a variable (E_NOTIMPL): a constant's value, or an
  instance variable read or written at its offset.
- RegisterTypeLibForUser and UnRegisterTypeLibForUser (they registered
  for the whole machine) use HKCU\Software\Classes, and the registered
  type library lookups (LoadRegTypeLib, QueryPathOfRegTypeLib) look there
  before the machine's classes, as Windows' merged HKEY_CLASSES_ROOT
  does.

Wine's oleaut32 typelib test: no failures.

Gate: test/tlbcreate-gate.sh (64- and 32-bit, test/tlbcreate-probe.c).
Mutants SG_MUTANT_FIXED_STATS, SG_MUTANT_NO_MEMBER_CUSTDATA,
SG_MUTANT_NO_VAR_INVOKE, SG_MUTANT_USER_IS_MACHINE (oleaut32/typelib.c).
